  "body": "SYNAPSE_NO_TLS behavior unexpected. SYNAPSE_NO_TLS=1 and SYNAPSE_NO_TLS=0 didn't work for federation behind a proxy-\r\n\r\nExpected behavior: \r\nSYNAPSE_NO_TLS=1 works behind a proxy and is also able to support federation connections.\r\nSYNAPSE_NO_TLS=0 works with certs in /data/homeservername.tls.key/crt with direct forwared port 8448.\r\n\r\n\r\nDetails:\r\nI setup a new server recently and decided to try this docker file.\r\nAs I like the idea of having everything behind a proxy (with it's on cert manager), I struggled with the installation as I chosed: SYNAPSE_NO_TLS= 1.\r\n\r\nAs stated more than once, the documentation of Synapse regarding the (federation)ports, the docker config  suggests that we can disable TLS and use 8008 instead for both (second -names: entry in homerserver.yaml).\r\n\r\nThis didn't work for me from federation perspective. So I set SYNAPSE_NO_TLS=0, using the valid proxy certs also on matrix host. Also, no incoming connect.\r\n\r\nSolution:\r\nAfter removing the env variable completely it seems to work (still with some regular timeouts in the logs).\r\n\r\n\r\nWish:\r\nImproved documentation about deployments behind proxies and better documentation regardings ports & tls in general. \r\nLet's encrypt can't be the answer for everything, as it doesn't fit in every environment.",
